Implemented the bowling scorer in `bowling.py` — a `BowlingGame` class with `roll(pins)` accumulating throws and `score()` doing a 10-frame index scan: strike = 10 + next two rolls, spare = 10 + next roll, open = frame pins. Tenth-frame fill balls fall out naturally from the same index walk.

